","tool_id":"call_89c2b16df424","agent_id":"main","sequence":57,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_cccc12869261","type":"reasoning","started_at":"2026-10-19T18:39:15.491255+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T18:39:26.284684+00:00","duration_ms":10793.423699913546,"text":"**Evaluating thumbnail dimensions**\n\nI'm considering the thumbnail size and whether to revise the header variant. I wonder if it should be set to 100% width. The current image size is too small, which could lead to a poor aspect ratio when expanded. I should check the documentation for any size specifications. It seems there's a preference for using a \"header\" variant that fits better, and I'll need to ensure that it's easy to read. I might create a summary with critical details and file listings as that could be helpful!**Finalizing deliverables**\n\nI need to keep the final summary concise. It’s important to emphasize that the highest value comes from calibrating the synchronization before adding more sensors. I shouldn't repeat the uncertainties of the scope.\n\nThe measurements prioritize the calibration and geometry of the clock without requiring new data acquisition. I also need to ensure the deliverables zip includes 19 files with summaries, names, and figures as specified. Lastly, I’ll note that I've prepared the final report with references to the original files, and there shouldn’t be any external links in the report. Once everything is accepted, my task will be complete!","source":"provider","provider_source":"model","reasoning_source":"provider_field","default_collapsed":true,"agent_id":"main","sequence":60,"stream_source":"live","channel":"provider_thinking:model:provider_field"},{"id":"live_call_04d9372977c1_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_04d9372977c1","agent_id":"main","sequence":61,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_62fb21418223_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_62fb21418223","agent_id":"main","sequence":63,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_9511983f43ab","type":"text","text":"## What is robust\n\n**The strongest conclusions concern what the instruments recorded, not a fully established smoke-transport mechanism.**\n\n- **Particles were strongly episodic.** The optical estimate rose from a morning mean of **1.43 µg/m³** to **3,538 µg/m³** in the largest minute. Exact smoke mass and particle size fraction remain unverified.\n- **The largest burst did not occur in locally calm air.** Screened horizontal wind averaged **7.35 m/s**, compared with **6.01 m/s** during 15:00–16:00. This does not resolve wind direction, stability or mixing.\n- **CO₂ and particles are not interchangeable tracers.** Only **4 of their top 10 minutes overlap**. Their association depends substantially on the window and averaging interval.\n- **Basic processing checks do not overturn those findings.** Removing partially gap-affected minutes changes full-window Pearson r only from **0.196 to 0.195**; corrected CO₂ packet parsing leaves rounded burn-day results unchanged.\n\nThese conclusions are supported by the [aligned observations](workspace-file:/D:/CLIO-Develop/ndp-showcases-20261019/konza/konza-aligned-minutes.csv) and [packet audit](workspace-file:/D:/CLIO-Develop/ndp-showcases-20261019/konza/konza-wind-co2-coverage.md). **Combustion-specific CO₂ enhancement, plume paths, transport lags, AQI, emissions and flux remain unestablished.**\n\n## What would improve the explanation most\n\n**First recover existing calibration, clock, inlet, survey and burn-operation logs.** Those may resolve important uncertainties without adding instruments.\n\nThen prioritize:\n\n1. **Synchronized upwind and downwind CO₂, particles and CO**, with shared intake locations where feasible, to distinguish background variation from plume enhancements.\n2. **Surveyed, north-referenced 3-D winds, stability observations and time-stamped fire-front imagery**, to test plume-crossing and dispersion explanations.\n3. **Size-resolved particles, reference filter mass and RH/temperature**, to constrain particle size, optical calibration and humidity effects.\n\n## Left for the collaborator\n\n**`konza-collaborator-handoff.zip`** contains the concise summary, both high-resolution figures, supporting tables, provenance, audit and reproduction instructions. The packaged comparison script reproduced all retained numerical results exactly.\n\nAlso available separately:\n- **`konza-collaborator-summary.md`**\n- **`figure-1-timeline.png`**\n- **`figure-2-association.png`**\n\nThe figures are shown above; open them at full size for labels and caveats. The original interactive views remain available.","agent_id":"main","sequence":65,"stream_source":"live","channel":"answer"},{"id":"part_67bf137b0823","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_e50a5b1639b84d898b6610a44c1897ab","agent_id":"main","sequence":66},{"id":"part_47860195c4f9","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_d07c48450d884e39b0fb86dd9cb3d8e1","agent_id":"main","sequence":67},{"id":"part_218f5df36537","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_4c7f661474e34d5aa38a6dcd2efa38e9","agent_id":"main","sequence":68},{"id":"part_d7c83663bbe6","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_f951c3f8d4884c97b048050c7761aa60","agent_id":"main","sequence":69}],"run_id":"a2120cfd-46d0-4d78-8f53-40d5d0754a9e","usage":{"input":3174090,"output":14193,"cache_read":2953472,"cache_write":0},"stop_reason":"end_turn","completed_at":"2026-10-19T18:40:15.925863+00:00"}],"tools":[{"id":"call_17e8286eda0f","session_id":"sess_b1bbf58c66a5","run_id":"6dfdf0f1-d306-4446-aabc-81dcfcde0d00","name":"connected_data_status","title":"Connected data","state":"succeeded","input":{},"output":{"accounts":[{"authenticated":false,"login_action":{"context":{"clio_id":"clio_303a9804ddda46528f38cd3f489d8b3f","workspace_id":"ws_6978effdcd75"},"name":"data_source/login/github"},"provider":"github","sign_in_available":true},{"authenticated":false,"login_action":{"context":{"clio_id":"clio_303a9804ddda46528f38cd3f489d8b3f","workspace_id":"ws_6978e