rces, core findings and export inputs","access_paths":null,"access_reason":"","background":false,"command":"Get-Content .tmp/clio-documents/konza_association_chart.py -TotalCount 15; Get-Content konza-burn-analysis.md -TotalCount 55; Get-Item konza-particle-co2-pairs.csv,konza-window-correlations.csv,konza-provenance.json | Select-Object Name,Length","cwd":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-showcases-20261019\\konza","max_output_bytes":6000,"timeout_s":30},"output":{"content":[],"structuredContent":{"command":"Get-Content .tmp/clio-documents/konza_association_chart.py -TotalCount 15; Get-Content konza-burn-analysis.md -TotalCount 55; Get-Item konza-particle-co2-pairs.csv,konza-window-correlations.csv,konza-provenance.json | Select-Object Name,Length","cwd":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-showcases-20261019\\konza","exit_code":0,"stderr":"","stderr_truncated":false,"stdout":"import altair as alt\nbase=alt.Chart(alt.NamedData('source')).encode(x=alt.X('particle_mean_ug_m3:Q',title='Particle minute mean (�g/m3, symlog)',scale=alt.Scale(type='symlog',constant=1,domain=[0,7000]),axis=alt.Axis(values=[0,1,10,100,1000,4000],format=',.0f')),y=alt.Y('CO2MFd_mean:Q',title='Dry CO2 minute mean (�mol/mol)',scale=alt.Scale(zero=False)))\ntips=[alt.Tooltip('local_label:N',title='CDT minute'),alt.Tooltip('particle_mean_ug_m3:Q',format=',.2f'),alt.Tooltip('CO2MFd_mean:Q',format='.2f'),alt.Tooltip('particle_rank:Q',title='Particle rank, largest = 1'),alt.Tooltip('co2_rank:Q',title='CO2 rank, largest = 1'),alt.Tooltip('particle_status:N'),alt.Tooltip('gap_seconds:Q',format='.2f')]\npoints=base.mark_circle(size=32,opacity=.65).encode(color=alt.Color('period:N',title='April 15 CDT',scale=alt.Scale(domain=['08:00-16:00','16:00-17:00','17:00-20:00','20:00-24:00'],range=['#529ec4','#dd8932','#8c77c7','#7caf72']),legend=alt.Legend(orient='bottom',columns=2)),tooltip=tips)\nlabels=base.transform_filter('(datum.particle_rank === 1 || datum.particle_rank === 5 || datum.co2_rank === 1 || datum.co2_rank === 5)').transform_calculate(display_label='substring(datum.local_label, 7, 12)').mark_text(align='left',dx=7,dy=-9,fontSize=12,color='#bfc8d0').encode(text='display_label:N')\nchart=(points+labels).properties(width=620,height=300).configure_axis(labelFontSize=12,titleFontSize=12).configure_view(stroke=None)\n\n# Konza burn observations and what they support\n\n## Colleague summary\nOn April 15, 2022, the W038 ES-642 recorded large, intermittent particle bursts, with lower-level elevation persisting into the evening. This is consistent with smoke-bearing air intermittently reaching W038 during the burn experiment. It is not proof of ignition time, the cause of every burst, prairie-wide exposure or a health-standard exceedance.\n\nThe previously unread large files have now been downloaded and scanned in full. Both CSAT3 wind and LI-7200 CO2 cover the burn day. Their observations provide context, but do not establish a plume trajectory, a calm-air accumulation mechanism, a combustion-specific CO2 enhancement, an emission factor or an eddy-covariance flux.\n\nAll local times use America/Chicago, CDT (UTC-05:00). Every interval is start-inclusive and end-exclusive. Reported averages are sample-weighted, not gap-adjusted exposure estimates.\n\n## Key measured figures\n| April 15 CDT interval | Particle mean (�g/m3) | LI-7200 dry CO2 mean (�mol/mol) | Screened CSAT3 horizontal speed mean (m/s) |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 08:00-11:00 | 1.43 | 435.27 | 4.94 |\n| 12:19-12:20 | 764.85 | 443.87 | 7.10 |\n| 15:00-16:00 | 3.18 | 449.95 | 6.01 |\n| 16:30-17:00 | 450.85 | 454.18 | 6.25 |\n| 16:41-16:42 | 3,538.36 | 455.10 | 7.35 |\n| 18:32-18:33 | 864.76 | 451.83 | 7.25 |\n| 19:00-20:00 | 7.36 | 445.91 | 5.55 |\n\nThe largest individual particle reading was **12,758 �g/m3 at 16:41:42.748 CDT**. The 16:41 minute contains 55 particle readings, 1,200 LI-7200 Data packets and 1,200 CSAT3 records; 128 flagged wind records were excluded, leaving 1,072 for its speed statistic. Min-max ranges in the views are observed variability, not confidence intervals.\n\n## What we can conclude\n- The particle change was episodic, not a smooth all-day rise. April 15 has 51,918 recorded readings from 08:00 to midnight: 199 (0.38%) exceed 1,000 �g/m3 and 2,573 (4.96%) exceed 100 �g/m3. These are descriptive sample fractions, not health thresholds or fractions of elapsed time.\n- Lower-level elevation also lingered. The 16:00-19:00 mean/median was 132.69/29 �g/m3; 19:00-24:00 was 7.73/6, compared with 1.43/1 at 08:00-11:00. Block summaries do not prove a continuously elevated plateau through unobserved intervals.\n- CO2 shows a modest local rise near the main particle burst. Its largest April 15 minute mean was 455.79 �mol/mol at 16:43, compared with 453.21 at 16:35. This is descriptive temporal concurrence, not a lag estimate or source attribution. A near-equal CO2 mean of 455.25 occurred at 16:22 while particles averaged only 2.60 �g/m3, so the two signals are not simply proportional.\n- The screened horizontal wind-speed mean at the particle-peak minute was 7.35 m/s, versus 6.01 over 15:00-16:00. These observations do not support a simple calm-air explanation. They do not rule out effects of turbulence, stability, source motion or spatially varying dispersion.\n\n## What we cannot conclude\n","stdout_spill":{"head_lines":36,"path":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-live-20261018\\home\\state\\workspaces\\2d41d4270aaeaaeb1be92b5f\\tool-output\\sess_b1bbf58c66a5\\sh_20261019T133437_e7dfc39e.stdout.txt","reason":"shell_output_spilled","relative_path":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-live-20261018\\home\\state\\workspaces\\2d41d4270aaeaaeb1be92b5f\\tool-output\\sess_b1bbf58c66a5\\sh_20261019T133437_e7dfc39e.stdout.txt","status":"spilled","tail":"\n## Provenance and reproducibility\nSource collection: NDP dataset `335fa1cb-d6d2-4e96-bc8e-c309d957b24d`, **NEON MDP / Sage / WIFIRE BP3D: Konza Prairie Burn Experiment**, publisher sage-neon. This is distinct from the separate classification-results dataset.\n\n| File | NDP resource ID | Interpretation used here |\n|---|---|---|\n| 21-W038.ndjson | 4e1ccb5d-aef9-4c06-846a-e45eb6d72fd1 | W038 `env.air_quality.conc`, `meta.sensor=es642`; mg/m3 multiplied by 1,000 |\n| 1-reading.sensor.csat3.pkl | 07a135d1-bcd3-4e12-aff5-1e91d667fe5e | MDP5 source 46586, readout_time, ux/uy/uz components and flags b12-b15 |\n\nName                          Length\n----                          ------\nkonza-particle-co2-pairs.csv  159847\nkonza-window-correlations.csv    841\nkonza-provenance.json          29377\n\n","tail_lines":15,"total_bytes":9652,"total_lines":69},"stdout_truncated":true,"timed_out":false,"timeout_s":30.0}},"presentation":{"action":"Run","summary":"","blocks":[{"id":"terminal","type":"terminal","media_type":"","text":"import altair as alt\nbase=alt.Chart(alt.NamedData('source')).encode(x=alt.X('particle_mean_ug_m3:Q',title='Particle minute mean (�g/m3, symlog)',scale=alt.Scale(type='symlog',constant=1,domain=[0,7000]),axis=alt.Axis(values=[0,1,10,100,1000,4000],format=',.0f')),y=alt.Y('CO2MFd_mean:Q',title='Dry CO2 minute mean (�mol/mol)',scale=alt.Scale(zero=False)))\ntips=[alt.Tooltip('local_label:N',title='CDT minute'),alt.Tooltip('particle_mean_ug_m3:Q',format=',.2f'),alt.Tooltip('CO2MFd_mean:Q',format='.2f'),alt.Tooltip('particle_rank:Q',title='Particle rank, largest = 1'),alt.Tooltip('co2_rank:Q',title='CO2 rank, largest = 1'),alt.Tooltip('particle_status:N'),alt.Tooltip('gap_seconds:Q',format='.2f')]\npoints=base.mark_circle(size=32,opacity=.65).encode(color=alt.Color('period:N',title='April 15 CDT',scale=alt.Scale(domain=['08:00-16:00','16:00-17:00','17:00-20:00','20:00-24:00'],range=['#529ec4','#dd8932','#8c77c7','#7caf72']),legend=alt.Legend(orient='bottom',columns=2)),tooltip=tips)\nlabels=base.transform_filter('(datum.particle_rank === 1 || datum.particle_rank === 5 || datum.co2_rank === 1 || datum.co2_rank === 5)').transform_calculate(display_label='substring(datum.local_label, 7, 12)').mark_text(align='left',dx=7,dy=-9,fontSize=12,color='#bfc8d0').encode(text='display_label:N')\nchart=(points+labels).properties(width=620,height=300).configure_axis(labelFontSize=12,titleFontSize=12).configure_view(stroke=None)\n\n# Konza burn observations and what they support\n\n## Colleague summary\nOn April 15, 2022, the W038 ES-642 recorded large, intermittent particle bursts, with lower-level elevation persisting into the evening. This is consistent with smoke-bearing air intermittently reaching W038 during the burn experiment. It is not proof of ignition time, the cause of every burst, prairie-wide exposure or a health-standard exceedance.\n\nThe previously unread large files have now been downloaded and scanned in full. Both CSAT3 wind and LI-7200 CO2 cover the burn day. Their observations provide context, but do not establish a plume trajectory, a calm-air accumulation mechanism, a combustion-specific CO2 enhancement, an emission factor or an eddy-covariance flux.\n\nAll local times use America/Chicago, CDT (UTC-05:00). Every interval is start-inclusive and end-exclusive. Reported averages are sample-weighted, not gap-adjusted exposure estimates.\n\n## Key measured figures\n| April 15 CDT interval | Particle mean (�g/m3) | LI-7200 dry CO2 mean (�mol/mol) | Screened CSAT3 horizontal speed mean (m/s) |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 08:00-11:00 | 1.43 | 435.27 | 4.94 |\n| 12:19-12:20 | 764.85 | 443.87 | 7.10 |\n| 15:00-16:00 | 3.18 | 449.95 | 6.01 |\n| 16:30-17:00 | 450.85 | 454.18 | 6.25 |\n| 16:41-16:42 | 3,538.36 | 455.10 | 7.35 |\n| 18:32-18:33 | 864.76 | 451.83 | 7.25 |\n| 19:00-20:00 | 7.36 | 445.91 | 5.55 |\n\nThe largest individual particle reading was **12,758 �g/m3 at 16:41:42.748 CDT**. The 16:41 minute contains 55 particle readings, 1,200 LI-7200 Data packets and 1,200 CSAT3 records; 128 flagged wind records were excluded, leaving 1,072 for its speed statistic. Min-max ranges in the views are observed variability, not confidence intervals.\n\n## What we can conclude\n- The particle change was episodic, not a smooth all-day rise. April 15 has 51,918 recorded readings from 08:00 to midnight: 199 (0.38%) exceed 1,000 �g/m3 and 2,573 (4.96%) exceed 100 �g/m3. These are descriptive sample fractions, not health thresholds or fractions of elapsed time.\n- Lower-level elevation also lingered. The 16:00-19:00 mean/median was 132.69/29 �g/m3; 19:00-24:00 was 7.73/6, compared with 1.43/1 at 08:00-11:00. Block summaries do not prove a continuously elevated plateau through unobserved intervals.\n- CO2 shows a modest local rise near the main particle burst. Its largest April 15 minute mean was 455.79 �mol/mol at 16:43, compared with 453.21 at 16:35. This is descriptive temporal concurrence, not a lag estimate or source attribution. A near-equal CO2 mean of 455.25 occurred at 16:22 while particles averaged only 2.60 �g/m3, so the two signals are not simply proportional.\n- The screened horizontal wind-speed mean at the particle-peak minute was 7.35 m/s, versus 6.01 over 15:00-16:00. These observations do not support a simple calm-air explanation. They do not rule out effects of turbulence, stability, source motion or spatially varying dispersion.\n\n## What we cannot conclude\n- ES-642 is an optical particle-mass estimate, not chemistry, CO or CO2. The installed size-selective inlet is undocumented; do not call this confirmed PM2.5/PM10 or calculate AQI. Smoke-specific calibration and full instrument-status screening are unavailable. Sensitivity is 1 �g/m3, so precise morning-to-peak ratios are misleading.\n- Raw BME680 resistance is gas-sensitive electrical resistance affected by gases and humidity, not a specific gas concentration or particulate measure.\n- Sensor geometry, north orientation, inlet/tubing delay, calibration operations and independently synchronized clocks have not been established. Raw CSAT3 components are not a defensible north-referenced plume trajectory. No arbitrary lag shift or background subtraction was applied.\n- CO2 is not combustion-specific; slow changes, biological exchange and instrument operations are alternatives. Coincidence alone cannot isolate burn emissions. No emission factor, regional exposure or flux is calculated.\n\n## Coverage and quality caveats\nThe particle series contains 212,045 readings over 65 hours, April 15 08:00 to April 18 00:59 CDT, approximately 1 Hz. Twelve whole minutes contain no readings; the longest inter-reading interval is 73.991 seconds. No interpolation fills those gaps. Nominal reported flow is 2.0 L/min; status flags for the particle channel are unavailable. Timestamps are publication/receipt timestamps, not independently verified acquisition times.\n\nCSAT3 contains 4,680,001 records. LI-7200 contains 4,679,516 archive records holding 4,679","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"Get-Content .tmp/clio-documents/konza_association_chart.py -TotalCount 15; Get-Content konza-burn-analysis.md -TotalCount 55; Get-Item konza-particle-co2-pairs.csv,konza-window-correlations.csv,konza-provenance.json | Select-Object Name,Length","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":"","exit_code":0},{"id":"saved-output-stdout","type":"link","media_type":"","text":"\n## Provenance and reproducibility\nSource collection: NDP dataset `335fa1cb-d6d2-4e96-bc8e-c309d957b24d`, **NEON MDP / Sage / WIFIRE BP3D: Konza Prairie Burn Experiment**, publisher sage-neon. This is distinct from the separate classification-results dataset.\n\n| File | NDP resource ID | Interpretation used here |\n|---|---|---|\n| 21-W038.ndjson | 4e1ccb5d-aef9-4c06-846a-e45eb6d72fd1 | W038 `env.air_quality.conc`, `meta.sensor=es642`; mg/m3 multiplied by 1,000 |\n| 1-reading.sensor.csat3.pkl | 07a135d1-bcd3-4e12-aff5-1e91d667fe5e | MDP5 source 46586, readout_time, ux/uy/uz components and flags b12-b15 |\n\nName                          Length\n----                          ------\nkonza-particle-co2-pairs.csv 