9T18:37:10.474256+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T18:37:11.045704+00:00"},{"id":"call_2a46b98cef67","session_id":"sess_b1bbf58c66a5","run_id":"a2120cfd-46d0-4d78-8f53-40d5d0754a9e","name":"shell_bash","title":"Bash","state":"succeeded","input":{"_clio_task_description":"Check summary length and final figure sizes","access_paths":null,"access_reason":"","background":false,"command":"$s=Get-Content collaborator-handoff/konza-collaborator-summary.md -Raw; ($s -split '\\s+').Count; Get-Item collaborator-handoff/*.png | Select-Object Name,Length","cwd":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-showcases-20261019\\konza","max_output_bytes":1000,"timeout_s":30},"output":{"content":[],"structuredContent":{"command":"$s=Get-Content collaborator-handoff/konza-collaborator-summary.md -Raw; ($s -split '\\s+').Count; Get-Item collaborator-handoff/*.png | Select-Object Name,Length","cwd":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-showcases-20261019\\konza","exit_code":0,"stderr":"","stderr_truncated":false,"stdout":"831\n\nName                      Length\n----                      ------\nfigure-1-timeline.png    2049324\nfigure-2-association.png  680898\n\n","stdout_truncated":false,"timed_out":false,"timeout_s":30.0}},"presentation":{"action":"Run","summary":"","blocks":[{"id":"terminal","type":"terminal","media_type":"","text":"831\n\nName                      Length\n----                      ------\nfigure-1-timeline.png    2049324\nfigure-2-association.png  680898\n\n","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"$s=Get-Content collaborator-handoff/konza-collaborator-summary.md -Raw; ($s -split '\\s+').Count; Get-Item collaborator-handoff/*.png | Select-Object Name,Length","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":"","exit_code":0}]},"duration_ms":1985.412359237671,"started_at":"2026-10-19T18:37:10.817268+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T18:37:12.802680+00:00"},{"id":"call_8be71311bd64","session_id":"sess_b1bbf58c66a5","run_id":"a2120cfd-46d0-4d78-8f53-40d5d0754a9e","name":"create_artifact","title":"Create Artifact","state":"succeeded","input":{"annotation":"","artifacts":[{"annotation":"Concise collaborator handoff with robust findings, limits and ranked evidence priorities.","content":"# Konza burn observations for a collaborator\n\n**Bottom line:** W038 recorded intermittent particle bursts during the April 15, 2022 burn experiment. Wind was not calm at the largest burst. CO₂ overlapped that burst but was not proportional to particles; attribution and transport mechanisms remain unresolved. Times below are CDT (UTC−05:00).\n\n## Conclusions that survive the checks\n\n- **Large bursts are robust features of the recorded optical signal.** Particle mean was 1.43 µg/m³ at 08:00–11:00 versus 3,538.36 in the 16:41 minute; the individual maximum was 12,758. This supports intermittent smoke-bearing air at W038, not verified smoke mass, ignition timing or the cause of every burst.\n- **A simple calm-air explanation is not supported by local speed.** Screened horizontal wind averaged 7.35 m/s during the peak minute versus 6.01 during 15:00–16:00. Direction, source conditions, stability and turbulence are not resolved by this comparison.\n- **Particle and CO₂ extremes overlap only partly.** Four of the top ten particle minutes were also top-ten CO₂ minutes among 958 paired minutes from 08:00–24:00. At 16:23, CO₂ ranked fifth (455.26 µmol/mol) while particles ranked 505th (3.52 µg/m³). Adjacent high minutes are not independent episodes.\n- **The association depends on analysis choices.** Pearson r is 0.196 for 08:00–24:00, 0.438 for 16:00–17:00 and −0.522 for 15:00–16:00. Full-window r rises to 0.319 with 15-minute averaging and 0.494 hourly. Extending 08:00–20:00 to midnight reduces Spearman ρ from 0.798 to 0.297.\n- **Basic processing checks do not overturn those findings.** Excluding 32 partially gap-affected minutes changes full-window r from 0.196 to 0.195. Corrected CO₂ packet parsing changes April 15 minute means by at most 0.000769 µmol/mol, leaving rounded findings unchanged.\n\n## Limits to keep attached\n\nES-642 inlet size cut, smoke calibration and full status screening are unverified; sensitivity is 1 µg/m³. Do not call this confirmed PM2.5/PM10 or calculate AQI. Across 65 hours, 12 particle minutes are empty and the longest inter-reading interval is 73.99 s; two empty minutes fall in the paired burn-day window. No filling was applied.\n\nWind statistics exclude 256 flagged samples, including 128 of 1,200 in the peak minute. Later negative CO₂ periods remain operationally unresolved and are excluded by restricting correlations to April 15. Unknown geometry, north orientation, clock synchronization and inlet delays preclude validated plume paths or lags. Particle timestamps are publication/receipt times. Correlation does not establish combustion-specific CO₂ enhancement, emission factors, exposure or flux; serial dependence and overlapping windows prevent independent-sample significance claims.\n\n## Highest-value next evidence\n\n**First recover deployment records:** surveyed positions/heights, orientation, clock logs, inlet/flow specifications, zero/span and valve-state logs, and burn-operation timing. Resolve negative CO₂ episodes before lag or covariance analysis. Existing wind and CO₂ already sample near 20 Hz.\n\n1. **Background and attribution:** synchronized upwind and multiple downwind measurements of CO₂, particles and a combustion tracer such as CO, with shared intake locations where feasible. These distinguish background changes from plume enhancements and strengthen, not guarantee, attribution.\n2. **Transport and mixing:** surveyed north-referenced 3-D winds at relevant heights, temperature/stability observations and time-stamped fire-front or thermal imagery. These test plume-crossing and dispersion explanations.\n3. **Particle validity:** co-located size-resolved particles, reference filter mass, RH/temperature and pre/post-event calibrations. These constrain size fraction, smoke optical response and humidity effects.\n\n## Key figures and evidence\n\n- **figure-1-timeline.png:** 08:00–20:00 minute means, observed ranges and coverage flags. Ranges are not confidence intervals; presence is not quality approval.\n- **figure-2-association.png:** paired minutes, peak/counterexample labels and window-specific Pearson/Spearman results. Particle axis is symlog; Pearson uses untransformed values.\n\nThe package retains full aligned and paired-minute tables, correlations, gaps, provenance, packet audit and derivative scripts/specifications. Means within bins are sample-weighted; correlations weight paired minutes/bins equally. Windows are start-inclusive/end-exclusive; no background subtraction or lag shifts were applied. Raw archives are not bundled; their IDs and hashes are retained.\n\n**Source:** NDP dataset `335fa1cb-d6d2-4e96-bc8e-c309d957b24d`, *NEON MDP / Sage / WIFIRE BP3D: Konza Prairie Burn Experiment*. W038 ES-642 is compared with MDP5 CSAT3 and LI-7200; co-location is not established.\n","kind":"report","name":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-showcases-20261019\\konza\\collaborator-handoff\\konza-collaborator-summary.md"},{"annotation":"Reviewed timeline export with particle, screened wind and dry CO2 minute means and observed ranges, plus gap and screening strips.","kind":"image","name":"figure-1-timeline.png","path":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-showcases-20261019\\konza\\collaborator-handoff\\figure-1-timeline.png"},{"annotation":"Reviewed paired-minute scatter and window sensitivity export, with peak/counterexample labels and descriptive Pearson and Spearman estimates.","kind":"image","name":"figure-2-association.png","path":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-showcases-20261019\\konza\\collaborator-handoff\\figure-2-association.png"}],"content":"","kind":"","name":"","path":"","pdf_preview":null,"purpose":"deliverable","used":["D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-showcases-20261019\\konza\\konza-aligned-minutes.csv","D:\\CLIO-Dev