2120cfd-46d0-4d78-8f53-40d5d0754a9e","name":"shell_bash","title":"Bash","state":"succeeded","input":{"_clio_task_description":"Add portable reproduction instructions and a numerical regression check","access_paths":null,"access_reason":"","background":false,"command":"@'\nreadme='''# Konza collaborator handoff\n\nStart with konza-collaborator-summary.md and the two PNG figures.\nThe original interactive views remain in the CLIO conversation; this archive contains portable static figures and evidence tables, not an offline interactive app.\n\n## Reproduce derivative calculations\nFrom the extracted package directory, run:\n    uv run --no-project python methods/reproduce_window_comparison.py\nThis standard-library script reads data/konza-aligned-minutes.csv and rewrites the paired-minute and window-correlation derivatives under data/. It also writes intermediate results under data/.tmp/. It does not rescan raw archives.\n\n## Rerender the figures\n    uv run --no-project --with vl-convert-python python methods/render_figures.py\nThe two self-contained Vega-Lite specifications include the plotted data. The original figure builder is retained for inspection and contains original workspace paths; use render_figures.py for portable rendering.\n\nThe full grid retains missing values, later suspect CO2 periods and sample counts. Correlation results concern only April 15, 08:00 to midnight CDT. Raw archives are excluded; data/konza-provenance.json retains NDP identities and source hashes. Some paths in the historical provenance and audit describe the original workspace, not this portable package.\n\nmanifest.json hashes the retained package files, excluding itself. No remote data or original source files were modified.\n'''\n(p/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')\n(methods/'render_figures.py').write_text(\"from pathlib import Path\\nimport vl_convert as vlc\\np=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nfor stem in ['figure-1-timeline','figure-2-association']:\\n   