rds and 482 double-packet records, totaling 4,679,998 packets and 4,679,998 unique measurement times. There were no missing packet Date/Time or CO2MFd fields, duplicate measurement timestamps or backward packet-time transitions. Of the extra packets, 480 were 50 ms later than the containing record readout_time and 2 were 100 ms later. All packets were included; no deduplication was needed. Counts changed in 458 minute bins. The 16:41 minute increases from 1,199 archive rows to 1,200 packets; its mean changes from 455.097306 to 455.097548 �mol/mol. The key table values are unchanged at two decimals. The maximum absolute minute-mean correction anywhere is 0.246949 �mol/mol, in the unresolved April 17 09:30 CDT interval. This correction does not resolve calibration or cross-instrument timing uncertainty.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe aligned export explicitly separates `co2_packets` / `CO2MFd_n` (embedded measurement time) from `co2_archive_records_by_readout_time` (outer archive timestamp). The packet-count CSV compares both definitions for every covered minute. April 15 minute-mean corrections are at most 0.000769 �mol/mol; the rounded key figures and qualitative interpretation are unchanged. Particle gaps and the half-open explorer boundary correction are unaffected by this CO2 parser fix.\r\n\r\n## Updated context-view review\r\nThe corrected three-panel particle/CO2/wind comparison and six-stream coverage were rendered locally and visually inspected at approximately 740-770 pixels wide. The comparison retains the low-particle/high-CO2 counterexample around 16:22; it does not select only the matching peak. The shared time axes, symlog particle scale, linear gas/wind scales and observed min-max ranges were checked. Client inspection resolved the corrected comparison to 60 rows and coverage to 3,240 rows. A whole-client capture timed out; component capture then found a hidden/busy viewer. The inspected viewer had a very narrow 183-pixel width. Therefore the revised context view is 